From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:09:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Warn when the inherited addon pins cannot be read

A process takes the addon versions its parent pinned from
XMAKE_ADDONS_PINNED; a value that does not deserialize was dropped
silently, so the child used the active versions with nothing said.
It now warns with the value and the reason and uses no inherited pins.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 xmake/core/package/addon.lua | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xmake/core/package/addon.lua b/xmake/core/package/addon.lua
index 971ae5dda..1283d7117 100644
--- a/xmake/core/package/addon.lua
+++ b/xmake/core/package/addon.lua
@@ -485,7 +485,12 @@ function addon._pinned()
         pinned = {}
         local inherited = os.getenv("XMAKE_ADDONS_PINNED")
         if inherited then
-            pinned = inherited:deserialize() or {}
+            local errors
+            pinned, errors = inherited:deserialize()
+            if not pinned then
+                utils.warning("XMAKE_ADDONS_PINNED(%s) is ignored, %s", inherited, errors or "it is invalid")
+                pinned = {}
+            end
         end
         addon._PINNED = pinned
     end
